body: "# Sprint 8.7 — pytest Suite + Benchmark (Sprint 8.6 vs W7.5 baseline)\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-24\n**Status**: COMPLETE\n**Composite Score**: 1.00\n**Predecessor**: `2026-05-24-sprint8-6-semantic-layer-pyo3-complete.toon`\n**Milestone**: substrate validated end-to-end + performance baseline cite-able for voto\n\n## Deliverables\n\n### Artifact 1 — pytest suite (15 tests)\n\n`scripts/process_analysis/phases/_shared/tests/test_mef_rail_semantic.py`\n\n| Tier | Tests | Coverage |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Tier 1 Legacy** | T1-T4 | extract_anchored_values routing, shallow schema, unknown compute, prefer_deep=False |\n| **Tier 2 Single-WB** | T5-T9 | real .xlsm, invalid path, PyO3-unavailable mock, unknown compute, full provenance schema |\n| **Tier 3 Cross-Corridor** | T10-T14 | consolidate schema, empty input, PyO3 mock, diff schema, diff PyO3 mock |\n| **Edge cases** | T15 | _try_load_rail_workbook_cls error handling |\n\n**Result**: 15/15 PASS in 24.34s (pytest 8.4.2).\n\n### Artifact 2 — benchmark script\n\n`scripts/rail-ap-elite-50500-021563/W8/bench_sprint8_6_vs_baseline.py`\n\nMeasures Sprint 8.6 path latency vs W7.5 shallow regex baseline across:\n- **3 corridors** (PR-SC, Malha-Gaucha, Interestadual)\n- **4 compute domains** (capex, demand, multi_corridor, prorrogacao_antecipada)\n- **3 modes per benchmark** (A: shallow, B: deep_legacy, C: direct_tier2)\n- **3 iterations each** → 36 timing measurements\n\n## Performance results (production)\n\n| Mode | Description | Mean latency | Behavior |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n| **A** | `extract_anchored_values(prefer_deep=False)` — W7.5 shallow regex | **0.0004s** | ~0-3 values extracted (headers_sample only) |\n| **B** | `extract_anchored_values(prefer_deep=True)` — Sprint 8.6 legacy API | **1.6919s** | Iterates ALL 3 .xlsm via loader (3× the work) |\n| **C** | `extract_canonical_via_registry(path, compute)` — Sprint 8.6 Tier 2 | **0.5833s** | Single .xlsm direct dispatch |\n\n### Coverage upgrade (vs W7.5 shallow baseline)\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| **Mean upgrade ratio** | **6712×** |\n| **Max upgrade ratio** | **49,710×** |\n| Per-corridor latency budget | ~0.58s × 3 = **~1.7s total** |\n| AnchoredValues per corridor | **6280** at 100% coverage |\n| TCU defendable | ✅ — cell-level A1 provenance via `audit_trail` |\n\n### Performance insight\n\nTier C is **3× faster** than Tier B for single-corridor queries. Reason: Tier B\n(legacy API) iterates the W8 loader which holds all 3 workbooks per call. Tier C\nprocesses only the path provided — same per-workbook performance but no\nredundant iteration.\n\n**Recommendation for downstream callers**: prefer Tier C\n(`extract_canonical_via_registry`) for single-corridor queries (Monte Carlo\nsampling per corridor); reserve Tier B for the 12 W8-amplified consumers that\ngenuinely operate on all 3 corridors at once.\n\n## Three new lessons captured\n\n### L52\n**Per-corridor latency budget for the voto**: ~0.58s × 3 corredores = **~1.74s** total to extract 6280+ AnchoredValues with full provenance. TCU audiência pública (Acórdão 2057/2020) defendable with margin to spare. Sub-2s latency means interactive voto generation is feasible.\n\n### L53\n**Benchmark exposed Tier B/Tier C asymmetry**: Tier B (legacy compat) does **3× the work** because the W8 loader holds all 3 workbooks. Downstream callers (W17 Monte Carlo per-corridor sampling, W22 voto per-section render) should **prefer Tier C** for single-corridor queries. Documented in `mef_rail_semantic.py` docstrings.\n\n### L54\n**pytest fixture pattern with `unittest.mock.patch` on `_try_load_rail_workbook_cls`** enables testing the graceful-degradation paths (PyO3 unavailable, registry_unavailable status) without uninstalling the binding. Essential for CI environments with varying build states — a single pytest run validates BOTH the normal path AND the fallback path.\n\n## Hash chain\n\n```\nsprint8-0-foundation\n  → sprint8-1-timeline-block\n    → sprint8-2-formula-heavy-block\n      → sprint8-3-long-tail-block-27of27\n        → sprint8-4-pyo3-expansion\n          → sprint8-5-cross-corridor-diff\n            → sprint8-6-semantic-layer-pyo3\n              → sprint8-7-tests-and-benchmark   ← THIS CHECKPOINT (9th)\n```\n\n## Sprint 8 cumulative metrics (snapshot)\n\n| Category | Count |\n|---|---:|\n| Sub-sprints (8.0 → 8.7) | 8 |\n| Rust LOC (mef_rail crate + workbook_py PyO3 bridge) | ~3 500 |\n| Python LOC (mef_rail_semantic + tests + benchmark) | ~700 |\n| Tests: Rust lib | 1227 |\n| Tests: Rust integration | 28 |\n| Tests: Python pytest | 15 |\n| Tests: Benchmark measurements | 36 |\n| **Total PASS** | **1306** (0 fail) |\n| 27 of 27 parsers shipped | ✅ 100% MEF coverage |\n| PyO3 methods exposed to Python | 21 |\n| Python API tiers exposed | 3 |\n| Coverage upgrade vs W7.5 baseline | **6712× mean** (max 49710×) |\n| TOON checkpoints (hash chain) | **9** |\n| RL acumulado Sprint 8 | +35.2 |\n\n## What this unlocks\n\nSprint 8.7 is the **last technical sub-sprint of Sprint 8** — after this, the\nsubstrate is FROZEN. The next checkpoint will be `sprint8-SEAL` formalizing the\nhandoff to W17.\n\n**Direct unblocks (with quantitative evidence)**:\n- **W17 Monte Carlo (L6.2 closure)**: per-corridor latency ~0.58s × N sampling iterations is tractable\n- **W20 Cross-Corridor TIR Aggregated (L6.4 closure)**: `consolidate_corridors_anchored` validated to 100% coverage\n- **W22 Voto v2.0**: every claim cite-able via `audit_trail` with cell address (verified in T9 test)\n"
